WHAT WOULD IT TAKE? — explicit requirements to unlock the blocked questions
====================================================================================================================================

  N7/N8  2L strategy after 1L immunotherapy (the top evidence gap)
     blocked by : sample size + residual calendar drift
     requirement: ~110 patients per arm for HR 1.5 at 80% power; REACH supplies 43 vs 51 overall and 23 vs 30 concurrently -> needs a MULTI-SITE consortium, or 3-5 more years of accrual

  N1/N12 Atezo/Bev vs STRIDE at 1L
     blocked by : positivity / channelling by liver function and prior TACE
     requirement: Child-Pugh B/C 11% vs 47% and prior TACE 17% vs 50%. Restricting to ALBI 1-2 + CP-A leaves 117 vs 55 but common support only 0.81 and 0.57 in the 2023-24 window. Needs chart-reviewed reason-for-choice, or reframing as a selection study

  N3 STRIDE vs Nivo/Ipi
     blocked by : near-deterministic selection (PS c-statistic 0.93-0.97)
     requirement: calendar era is perfectly matched (year-SMD 0.02) — the obstacle is clinical, not temporal. Would need the documented rationale from clinic notes to model the choice

  Any AFP-driven question (e.g. ramucirumab for AFP >=400)
     blocked by : AFP measured at only 18% (-14d) to 28% (-90d) of decision indices
     requirement: AFP is ordered too rarely around the decision to support an AFP-stratified design

  Tumour burden / RECIST response as exposure or outcome
     blocked by : regex cannot extract target-lesion size or response reliably
     requirement: LLM-based or manual abstraction of the 709 retrievable pre-index liver reports

  N11 bevacizumab discontinuation while continuing atezolizumab
     blocked by : borderline sample (19-26 vs 51-58) and immortal-time bias
     requirement: clone-censor-weight or sequential-trial emulation design; pooled multi-site N

  N4/N6 TKI vs ICI comparisons
     blocked by : irreducible calendar separation (median index-date gap 539 and 984 days)
     requirement: NOT repairable in a single-centre cohort — do not pursue as a survival comparison

