Four v8 bugs corrected
med_admin.generic_name is NULL for IV oncology drugs — v8 silently lost 320 nivolumab / 182 bevacizumab / 176 atezolizumab patients. v9 filters medication_name.
MAR action values: real distribution is New Bag 6,920 vs Given 694. v8's ('Given','Administered','Completed') filter discarded most infusions.
No ord_status filter — v8 counted Suspend/Discontinued TKI orders as exposure (lenvatinib 165 → 124 active).
Mixed timelines — v8 used Beacon plan dates for ICIs but order dates for oral TKIs, artificially pushing TKIs to later lines. This fully explains the v8 anomaly of 165 lenvatinib-exposed but only 5 at 1L.
Research-opportunity verdict (12 candidate decision nodes, 7 gates each)
TIER 1 (comparative effectiveness feasible) — N5 1L ICI-combination vs ICI-monotherapy (285 vs 132). Statistically feasible but low clinical equipoise: single-agent PD-1 is no longer a guideline 1L option.
TIER 2 (treatment-selection study only) — N1 Atezo/Bev vs STRIDE (144 vs 80; year-SMD 0.03) and N2 Atezo/Bev vs Nivo/Ipi. Blocked for causal survival inference by positivity, not by sample size.
TIER 3 (era-confounded, not repairable) — N4 Lenvatinib vs Sorafenib, N6 ICI vs TKI (median index-date gap 539 and 984 days), N7/N8/N9 second-line sequencing.
TIER 4 (underpowered) — N3 STRIDE vs Nivo/Ipi, N10, N12.
The clinically hottest question — 2L strategy after 1L immunotherapy (N7, equipoise VERY HIGH, no RCT exists) — fails on N: 43 TKI vs 51 ICI-based, falling to 23 vs 30 concurrently, smallest detectable HR 2.53. It requires a multi-site consortium.

Recommended primary project
Determinants and consequences of first-line Atezo/Bev vs STRIDE selection in advanced HCC — two linked aims on one cohort.

Aim 1 (fully feasible): treatment-selection model, outcome = regimen chosen, 1L starts 2023–2026, 144 vs 80 (59 vs 40 concurrent, year-SMD 0.03). Publishable alone; PS c-statistic 0.82 shows selection is highly predictable from liver function, varices/bleeding risk, autoimmune history and prior locoregional therapy.
Aim 2 (hypothesis-generating): IPTW survival comparison trimmed to the PS common-support region (retains 86%), pre-specified detectable HR ≥ 1.66, reported with a formal positivity caveat.
Covariate measurability at a treatment decision (n=806 indices)
Research-grade: comorbidity ICD 100%, death/follow-up 100% (63% died, median FU 347 d), ALBI 93.8%, liver panel 93.1%, pre-index liver imaging flags 88.0% (PVTT/extrahepatic/multifocal, 96% precision), Beacon discontinuation reason 86.0%, ECOG from notes 60.7% (100% audit precision), BCLC 44.9%, Child-Pugh 42.4% (97% precision).

Not usable: AFP 19.7% (kills any AFP-stratified design such as ramucirumab for AFP ≥400), structured ECOG 1.5%, and tumour size / RECIST response — regex failed adjudication, needs LLM or manual abstraction of the 709 retrievable reports.

